	sudo chown pgbackrest:pgbackrest /etc/pgbackrest.conf;
	sudo -u pgbackrest chmod 640 /etc/pgbackrest.conf;
	
Setup pgbackrest for DB Node:


	sudo dnf install -y https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/epel-release-latest-9.noarch.rpm
	sudo dnf makecache;
    	sudo dnf -y install pgbackrest;

	Put below data in file /etc/pgbackrest.conf
	sudo vi /etc/pgbackrest.conf

	[global]
repo1-host=aman-external1
repo1-host-user=pgbackrest
repo1-path=/data/backup

[standalone]
pg1-path=/var/lib/postgresql/16/data


	sudo chown postgres:postgres /etc/pgbackrest.conf;
	sudo -u postgres chmod 600 /etc/pgbackrest.conf;

	Add below line of code in postgresql.conf

	sudo vi /var/lib/postgresql/16/data/postgresql.conf
	archive_mode = on
archive_command = 'pgbackrest --config=/etc/pgbackrest.conf --stanza=standalone archive-push %p'

	
	sudo systemctl restart alloydbomni-16
	
	

Set up passwordless SSH setup. 

To enable remote backups and restores, the pgbackrest and postgres users require reciprocal passwordless SSH access.

Login to Backup VM and DB VM and run below command to generate ssh key
By running below command
sudo -u -i postgres / sudo -u -i pgbackrest 
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 2048 -f ~/.ssh/id_rsa

Copy id_rsa.pub from one VM to Another VM to this file vi ~/id_rsa.pub
Then run below command on both VM
cat ~/id_rsa.pub >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

Verify passwordless ssh access using below command

ssh pgbackrest@{{BACKUP_HOST}}
ssh postgres@{{DB_NODE}}


Login To Backup VM

	Create Stanza on Backup VM using below command

	sudo -u pgbackrest pgbackrest --config=/etc/pgbackrest.conf --stanza=standalone stanza-create
	sudo -u pgbackrest pgbackrest --config=/etc/pgbackrest.conf --stanza=standalone check


